      "message": "Highlight code on the server\n\nA file, a diff and a README each render in a frame of their own, and\nthe code in them is highlighted by the forge rather than by a script.\nThe highlighter walks each file with the grammar's own state, so a\nblock comment stays a comment on its second line, and writes every\ntoken as a span named by the grammar's scope; the stylesheet gives the\nfew that carry meaning a colour in each theme. Nothing is inline, and\nthe content policy stays as it was. Files past half a megabyte render\nplain and say so. The bundled grammars lack TOML, which every Rust\nrepository has, so a small one rides with the binary.\n\nThe code frame heads a file with its path, its length, its language\nand the change that landed it, and offers Blame; blame renders in the\nsame frame with the state dot and the attribution column. The diff\nframe heads each file with its path and its plus and minus counts,\nheads each hunk with the line range it covers rather than the index\nline, numbers both sides, and marks the words that changed between a\ndeleted line and the added line that replaced it. The README is a\npanel of prose whose fenced code is highlighted like a file.\n\nChange-Id: Icode0127\nTask: t-7c7a5vtxkyc0dw0ktnvg70dz56\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
